# Module readme

This readme does not explain what the functions are more so the calling convetion used in this standard library and module.

- public functions, struct, enums or anything of that sort visible outside of module are denoted via camelCase as in
  most cases users will write in snake case hence they will not have much of namespace issue.

- Funtions we only use onces will only be in local functions scope.

- Except OS module exposing global constants is not allowed.

- When something is guaranteed that it must be a constant it uses :: declaration

- Comments is always at the begining before the function explaining what it does.

- EnumFlag members always start with capital letter.